1%2FSG-1%2FME1%20review%20solutions.pdf)" :db/ensure :tutorial/validate} {:db/id "5308d490-2910-58d4-a5e8-43c378e00e2b" :tutorial/id #uuid "5308d490-2910-58d4-a5e8-43c378e00e2b" :tutorial/title "Study direction" :tutorial/content "Source question: Review item 1, PDF page 1.\n\nReview **all lecture materials and written homeworks**; the source says these form a large portion of the review. This numbered item is a study direction, not a separate mathematical question. The supplied solutions point to in-class activity and written-homework solutions in the Canvas modules." :db/ensure :tutorial/validate} {:db/id "be7fb99a-bfe6-55a5-ada2-d01967181093" :question/id #uuid "be7fb99a-bfe6-55a5-ada2-d01967181093" :question/problem "**(a)** Could a system with five linear equations and three variables have infinitely many solutions?\n\n**(d), as applied to this part:** Provide an example, or explain why such a system is impossible." :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "6d38c50f-3ac5-5a3a-89fa-bda324be4120" :question/id #uuid "6d38c50f-3ac5-5a3a-89fa-bda324be4120" :question/problem "**(b)** Could such a system have no solutions?\n\n**(d), as applied to this part:** Provide an example, or explain why such a system is impossible." :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "1d1d7b78-9b64-5efc-81ff-7e1ff1731707" :question/id #uuid "1d1d7b78-9b64-5efc-81ff-7e1ff1731707" :question/problem "**(c)** Could such a system have a unique solution?\n\n**(d), as applied to this part:** Provide an example, or explain why such a system is impossible." :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d72836b2-64a1-5cec-898f-b0ea63aee498" :step/id #uuid "d72836b2-64a1-5cec-898f-b0ea63aee498" :step/content "be7fb99a-bfe6-55a5-ada2-d01967181093" :step/next "089c7125-f4ce-59fe-b764-abd66762b7ea" :db/ensure :step/validate} {:db/id "089c7125-f4ce-59fe-b764-abd66762b7ea" :step/id #uuid "089c7125-f4ce-59fe-b764-abd66762b7ea" :step/content "6d38c50f-3ac5-5a3a-89fa-bda324be4120" :step/next "8900463b-dcf5-5499-b1c2-